The Skyline Developers brand—the driving force behind the 10 coastal standalone homes at 5 & 7 Calder Place in Glendowie—operates under a series of localized entity structures, primarily directed and led by property developer Ashish Kapoor. [1, 2]

The Founder & Ownership

The Director: According to the New Zealand Companies Office, the managing entity behind the project is Skyline Developers Glendowie Limited, which was incorporated in June 2025. The sole registered director and principal owner is Ashish Kapoor. [1, 2]
The Brand Journey: Skyline Developers is not a brand new entity; it was originally established internationally in 2011. After delivering hundreds of homes, apartments, and commercial sections globally, the company expanded its operations directly into the New Zealand residential property space. [1]


Where They Live and Study

Where They Live: Ashish Kapoor lives locally in Epsom / Mount Eden, Auckland. His primary residential addresses and registered offices are anchored in these affluent central Auckland neighborhoods. [1, 2]
Where They Study & Base: While his early historical university or school details are kept strictly private, his active corporate footprint is deeply connected to Auckland's property landscape. The development team's design and build supervisors operate under New Zealand Licensed Building Practitioner (LBP) standards to deliver their specialized medium-density family packages. [1, 2, 3]


Where They Bank and Eat

Where They Bank: Their project infrastructure, land acquisitions, and construction drawdowns are routed through major New Zealand commercial institutional lenders, operating under corporate accounting and advisory partnerships via firm nodes based in Epsom and Greenlane, Auckland.
Where They Eat & Spend Time: Because the developer's main offices are located around Mount Eden and Epsom—and their primary build pipelines sit tightly within East Auckland (including Point England, St Johns, Glen Innes, and Glendowie)—the group's operational hub sits amidst the cafes and local dining scenes of Mount Eden Village, alongside coastal dining spots in St Heliers and Mission Bay where they meet with real estate agencies like Bayleys and Barfoot & Thompson to clear their high-end builds. [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]


The Glendowie Calder Place Build

The project at 5 & 7 Calder Place represents one of Skyline's premium boutique collections. Rather than putting up typical attached townhouses, they used the 1,625 square meter site to forge 10 standalone, freestanding architectural homes


 complete with 2.7m stud heights, private landscaped gardens, and Bosch-fitted kitchens designed specifically to frame coastal views of the Hauraki Gulf. [1, 2, 3, 4]
